# Homepage speed

`/` renders per request (root layout reads the cart cookie). Building its
product lists parses every brand catalogue (hundreds of MB) — uncached, cold
starts hit ~15s TTFB (Sep 2026 incident).

- Homepage product data must come from `src/lib/homepage-data.ts`
  (`unstable_cache`, trimmed card fields, 1h TTL, keyed per deployment).
  Do not call `getCollection100`, `loadAllBrandCatalogs`,
  `getHomepageCategoryProducts` or `getProductsByCategory` directly from
  `src/app/page.tsx` or components it renders. Add new homepage sections as
  another cached function in `homepage-data.ts`.
- Keep `@/data/products` out of the static import graph of `app/layout.tsx`
  and `app/page.tsx`: anything imported there is bundled into the route chunk
  and parsed on every cold boot (~9s with the catalogues). The layout reads the
  cart badge via `@/lib/cart-count` (cookie only) — never `@/lib/cart-server`.
  `homepage-data.ts` loads products with `await import()` for the same reason.
- Cache only what the page renders (`toProductCardProduct`), never full
  catalogue arrays — Vercel Data Cache items are capped at 2MB.
- Bump the `-vN` cache key when the cached shape changes.
- `.github/workflows/homepage-speed-guard.yml` pings `/` every 10 min (keeps
  it warm) and fails if TTFB > 8s. A failing run means a regression — fix it.
- Ship risky homepage/layout changes via a preview branch first
  (`scripts/ship-home-cache.sh` pattern): a failed build on `main` blocks all
  deploys, including catalogue syncs.
- Making the root layout static (client cart badge + ISR) was tried and failed
  the Vercel build late (prerender stage, cause not captured). Re-attempt only
  on a preview branch with the build log in hand.
